-- title:
--   Hereditary subalgebras of the unitization generated by elements of $A$ lie in $A$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a C*-algebra, not necessarily unital, and let $\tilde A=\mathbb{C}\oplus A$ be its unitization, whose elements are pairs $(\lambda,x)$ with $\lambda\in\mathbb{C}$, $x\in A$, multiplied by $(\lambda,x)(\mu,x')=(\lambda\mu,\ \lambda x'+\mu x+xx')$; an element $x\in A$ is identified with $(0,x)$. For an element $h$ of a C*-algebra $B$ write
--   $$\operatorname{Her}_B(h)=\overline{\{\,h\,b\,h^*:\ b\in B\,\}}.$$
--   Then for every $a\in A$ and every $z=(\lambda,x)\in\tilde A$,
--   $$z\in\operatorname{Her}_{\tilde A}(a)\ \Longrightarrow\ \lambda=0\ \text{ and }\ x\in\operatorname{Her}_A(a).$$
--   No positivity or norm condition on $a$ is required.
--
--   Thus the closed subalgebra of $\tilde A$ generated by an element of $A$ does not see the adjoined unit: it is contained in $A$, inside $\operatorname{Her}_A(a)$. This is what allows results proved for unital C*-algebras, applied inside $\tilde A$, to return elements of the original algebra $A$; it is used in this way in the non-unital shrinking lemma.
--
--   **Formalization Note** For `z : Unitization ℂ A`, the scalar part $\lambda$ is `z.fst` and the $A$-part $x$ is `z.snd`. Spectral-order instances on $A$ and $\tilde A$ are in scope, but the order plays no role in the statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Shrinking.lean#L158-L173

